# A rhinestone: lead-crystal glass (LLF1, the glass of cut-crystal jewellery) coated with a film of
# titania, titanium dioxide, the way coated stones are given their sparkle and colour. The film's
# index is the measured, dispersive glass:titania (2.92 at 360 nm, 2.44 at 550, 2.34 at 830).
# A coating does not change how the stone refracts or how much fire it throws -- both come from
# the glass inside -- it changes what the surface reflects: bare, this glass reflects 4.7 % face-on.
# At 250 nm the film reflects cyan face-on, blue at 30 degrees and violet past 50, so the colour
# changes from facet to facet. Other thicknesses, face-on: 60 nm a bright neutral mirror (34 %, the
# most sparkle, no colour); 80 nm gold; 100 nm pink; 130 nm deep blue; 160 nm green. Set
# `film_thickness` to choose. A clear coating: the stone refracts, so give it a closed shape.
# aliases: titania-glass titania-rhinestone tio2-coating
type thinfilm
ior            glass:lead-crystal
film_ior       glass:titania
film_thickness 250
